{"name":"Grey","hex":"#808080","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Grey","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname transferred from the nickname, alternative spelling of Gray.","A placename:\nA rural municipality (the Rural Municipality of Grey) in south-central Manitoba, Canada, named after Albert Grey, 4th Earl Grey.\nA river in the West Coast Region, South Island, New Zealand; in full, Grey River.\nA territorial authority, Grey District, on the West Coast, New Zealand, the successor of Grey County.\nEllipsis of Grey County."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of the Royal Scots Greys, a cavalry regiment of the British Army from 1707 to 1971."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Grey_Longhaired_Female_Cat.jpg/330px-Grey_Longhaired_Female_Cat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Grey_Longhaired_Female_Cat.jpg/330px-Grey_Longhaired_Female_Cat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrey_Longhaired_Female_Cat.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Whistlers_Mother_high_res.jpg/500px-Whistlers_Mother_high_res.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail